    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0164" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg80"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1236.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As will be seen by the inclosed copies of
                    translations from the Chihli Gazette of March 18, an attempt has been made in
                    the district. of Yu-t’ien, about 100 miles east of Peking, to reorganize the
                    Boxer association, but was promptly suppressed by the energetic action of the
                    viceroy.</p>
                <p>Several soldiers lost their lives in the attempt to arrest the criminals, but 7
                    of the criminals were killed and 10 more arrested, who are ordered beheaded and
                    their heads exposed where the organization started.</p>
                <p>Only such prompt and severe measures will prevent similar organizations in other
                    localities, and it is hoped and believed that Yuan Shih’k’ai will continue as he
                    has begun.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d88-a1.xml" xpointer="d88-a1"/>
